TIP:  For the intro, pick the note and strum the chord.  So untransposed pick the 5th string (a) and strum the (A) and repeat this pattern through "Sugar".  Then there's a quick (D) - (E) - (A) and you return to the a - (A) pattern for "tell them who we are".  Then, while still holding (A), pick the covered 2nd string (c#) twice, lift off the second string and pick it once (b), and then pick the covered 3rd string (a).

TIP:  After the intro the (A) |D| - (A) bit is meant to be played over the top of any spoken lyrics in parenthesis.

TIP:  The |E| in brackets before "cover" is one strum and then nothing until the next (A) on "Stone."  On the final "stone" strike the |A| hard and let it sustain through the spoken outro.
 

